                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "97491994",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198115485180",
                            "num_reviews": 2,
                            "playtime_forever": 1804,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 30,
                            "last_played": 1628974341
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "So played today for first time after a few updates. First this is NOT the game I purchased, AT ALL. I know it's early access and I expect some changes in gameplay etc, but this is a completely different game, even a different genre. It went from a dungeon crawler to a serious sam/ COD clone, with no tutorial, no controller explanations and horrible interface. It took me forever to figure out how to reload, I still don't know how to swap weapons. If you're going to completely scrap a game and start over (name and all) then just abandon the project and make the new game on it's own don't fob it off on early access purchasers.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1628868625,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1628868625,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 17,
                        "votes_funny": 3,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.6868517398834229,
                        "comment_count": 0,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": true,
                        "developer_response": "We're sorry you're not happy with the direction the game has taken over the last few updates and thanks for letting us know.\n\nIt was a hard decision but drastic changes needed to happen to make the game fun. We gathered a lot of feedback and tried many things to make the game work with the old direction but it just wasn't fun no matter how hard we tried. Once we added the new zombie game mode we got a lot of great feedback and people enjoyed it, so it just made sense make that the main focus.\nThe base mechanics of the game are still the same and all magic abilities have been converted to weapons that work the same way.\nTelekinesis magic -> gravity gun; fire magic -> flame thrower and so on.\n\nWe added another branch with the legacy version of the game on it you can still play through steam.\nRight click on Monster Showdown -> Properties -> Betas and select the `classic` branch from the drop down menu. This should trigger your game to re-download the old files. Save files are separate so there shouldn't be any issues.\n\nIf you want to request a refund you can do that here: \nhttps://help.steampowered.com/en/faqs/view/784C-923B-A4A1-C825\nIf you give them a good reason it should still work even if you own the game for more than 14 days and have played over 2 hours.",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1628928796,
                        "primarily_steam_deck": false,
                        "refunded": false
                    }
